Privacy Policy – Mixed Match
Last updated: August 19, 2026
MixedMatch is a free game developed by Jussi Games.
Information We Collect
MixedMatch may collect and process the following information:
Information you provide

A player display name (for example when you enter a name in the game). This name may be shown on in-game and online leaderboards.

Information collected automatically

An anonymous player identifier created by Unity Authentication (used to save and display your scores; it is not your real name, email, or phone number)
Game scores and related gameplay results submitted to online leaderboards
Basic technical data that may be processed by Unity Gaming Services when the game connects to the internet 
(for example IP address as part of normal service operation)

The game does not require you to create an account with email or password, and it does not ask for your phone number or precise location.
How We Use Information
We use this information to:

Display local and online leaderboards
Save high scores and game progress
Operate and improve the game’s online features

Data Storage
On your device
Game settings, local high scores, and similar data may be stored locally on your device (for example using the device’s local storage).
This data stays on your device unless you clear the app data or uninstall the game.
Online services
When online features are used, scores and your chosen display name may be sent to Unity Gaming Services (Unity Technologies) so that global leaderboards can work.
Unity processes this data according to its own privacy terms and policies.
Third-Party Services
Mixed Match uses the following third-party services:

Unity Gaming Services (including Authentication and Leaderboards) — to sign you in anonymously and to store/display leaderboard scores and display names

These services may process data (such as an anonymous player ID, display name, scores, and technical connection data) on servers operated by Unity.
For more information, see Unity’s privacy documentation:
https://unity.com/legal/privacy-policy
MixedMatch does not sell your personal information.
Children’s Privacy
MixedMatch is suitable for a general audience. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children for marketing or profiling.
Online leaderboards may show a display name and score chosen or generated in the game. If you are a parent or guardian and believe a child has
provided information that should be removed from leaderboards, contact us using the details below.
Data Retention

Local data remains on your device until you clear app data or uninstall the game
Online leaderboard entries are retained as long as the leaderboard service and the game’s online features remain active,
or until removed in accordance with our or Unity’s practices

Your Choices

You can play many parts of the game without using a custom name (a default name may be used)
You can clear local data by clearing the app storage or uninstalling the game
Online leaderboard data is tied to an anonymous player ID on the device; uninstalling the app does not always delete online leaderboard entries automatically

Changes to This Privacy Policy
This Privacy Policy may be updated if the game or its data practices change. The “Last updated” date at the top will be revised when changes are made.
The updated policy will be posted on this page.
